'''''Adonis microcarpa''''', commonly known as '''small-fruit pheasant's-eye''' or '''red chamomile''',  is an annual [[herbaceous plant]]. The species is native to western [[Asia]] and southern [[Europe]] and is naturalised in [[Australia]].<ref name=GRIN>{{GRIN | accessdate=29 May 2011}}</ref> It grows to 50&nbsp;cm high, has finely divided foliage and red flowers with black centres.<ref name=Viridans>{{cite book |title=Wild Plants of Victoria (database)|year=2009 |publisher=Viridans Biological Databases & Department of Sustainability and Environment}}</ref>

